  "comments": [
    {
      "path": ".claude/hooks/guard-shell-writes.sh",
      "content": "These options do not all change Git's working directory. For example, `git --work-tree=/project --git-dir=/tmp/repo.git reset --hard` overwrites files in `/project`, but the final `--git-dir` makes `here` external and bypasses the guard. Relative option values are also incorrectly resolved against previously supplied metadata/worktree paths rather than the effective cwd. Track cwd, Git directory, and explicit worktree separately, and check the effective worktree independently of option order.",
      "existing_code": "          -C|--git-dir|--work-tree) resolve \"$here\" \"${toks[i+1]:-.}\"; here=$res; ((i+=2)) ;;\n          --git-dir=*|--work-tree=*) resolve \"$here\" \"${toks[i]#*=}\"; here=$res; ((i++)) ;;",
      "start_line": 98,
      "end_line": 99,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": ".claude/hooks/guard-shell-writes.sh",
      "content": "Git accepts an attached `-C` argument, but `-C/project` reaches this fallback without updating `here`. With an outside initial cwd, `git -C/project reset --hard` is therefore allowed even when `/project` is the protected worktree. Handle `-C*` by resolving the suffix just as for the separate-argument form.",
      "existing_code": "          *) ((i++)) ;;",
      "start_line": 101,
      "end_line": 101,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": ".claude/hooks/guard-shell-writes.sh",
      "content": "Leaving `cur` unchanged for `cd -` makes the tracked directory incorrect. Starting in the project, `cd /tmp; cd -; git reset --hard` returns to the project in the shell but leaves `cur=/tmp`, so the destructive reset is allowed. Track the previous directory alongside `cur` and swap them for `cd -`.",
      "existing_code": "      elif [[ \"${toks[i]}\" != - ]]; then resolve \"$cur\" \"${toks[i]}\"; cur=$res; fi ;;",
      "start_line": 92,
      "end_line": 92,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": ".claude/hooks/guard-shell-writes.sh",
      "content": "When `out` is empty, this requests an array slice of length -1, which raises a Bash expansion error rather than resolving the path. Valid paths such as `/../project` should resolve to `/project`, but can interrupt the hook before it emits a denial. Only pop a component when the array is nonempty; otherwise retain `/`. Add a root-boundary regression case on Bash 3.2.",
      "existing_code": "      ..) out=(\"${out[@]:0:${#out[@]}-1}\") ;;",
      "start_line": 58,
      "end_line": 58,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
